{"path": "summary.md", "content": "**Latent Camera** is a high-performance, raw-processing Android camera application built with Jetpack Compose for the UI layer and the Camera2 API for low-level sensor access. Its core architecture centers on a custom OpenGL ES pipeline (`LivePreview` + `GLSurfaceView`) that renders a live viewfinder and executes real-time ISP operations—including demosaicing (CFA pattern handling), white balance correction, spatial denoising, false-color visualization, auto-levels, and highlight recovery—directly on the GPU. A dedicated `SensorCapture` module acquires raw sensor frames and extracts metadata (ISO, shutter speed, AWB gains, color matrix, flicker detection) via `ImageReader`, feeding them asynchronously into the rendering thread. Performance is actively managed through Android's Dynamic Performance Framework (ADPF), which boosts thread priorities and enables sustained performance mode for the GL, ISP, and capture-executor threads.

Functionally, the app supports both still capture (tap or volume-up) and video recording (long-press or volume-down, with a drag-to-lock gesture for hands-free recording). It handles multi-lens devices with physical camera switching, digital zoom, and front/rear camera selection. A comprehensive settings overlay exposes manual controls for ISO, exposure time, exposure compensation, AE lock, OIS toggling, and pipeline parameters (denoise mode, false color, histogram, log range, color saturation). Captured photos are saved to the Media Store with full EXIF metadata (GPS, focal length, aperture, software tag). Additional features include GPS geotagging via `LocationTracker`, a raw-preview comparison button, a debug overlay showing frame processing time and battery draw, and an external broadcast receiver for third-party video-toggle triggers.
